IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-domain`
IMPORT `cat-time`
IMPORT `cat-part1-preliminary`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA) — PART 4, ADMINISTRATION AND ENFORCEMENT (ss 42-75),
-- with Cat Regulations 2012 regs 26-30 and Schedule 2 (modified penalties).
--
-- Source: inputs/cat-act-2011.txt lines 466-682; inputs/cat-regulations-2012.txt
-- lines 236-245, 626-697.

§ `Part 4 — Administration and enforcement`

§§ `Division 1 — Administration`

§§§ `42. Administration by local governments`

-- s 42: "A local government is to administer its local laws and may do all
-- other things that are necessary or convenient to be done for, or in
-- connection with, performing its functions under this Act." INERT: a
-- general grant of power, with nothing to compute.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 42
GIVETH A STRING
`s 42` MEANS "A local government is to administer its local laws and may do all other things that are necessary or convenient to be done for, or in connection with, performing its functions under this Act."

§§§ `43. Places to be regarded as within district`

-- s 43(1): a Governor's approval under s 80 carries the Local Government
-- Act 1995 s 3.19 approval with it. INERT here (no rule computes Governor's
-- approvals).
-- s 43(2): "For the purposes of the performance of a function under this Act
-- by an authorised person appointed or designated by a local government, the
-- district of the local government is to be regarded as including — (a) any
-- part of the State into which the authorised person has pursued a cat or
-- person; and (b) any part of the State in which the authorised person has
-- performed a function in relation to an offence against this Act that
-- occurred, or that the authorised person believes, or suspects, on
-- reasonable grounds occurred, in the district of the local government that
-- appointed or designated the authorised person."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 43(2)
GIVEN `in the district`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `pursued a cat or person there`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `performing a function there for an offence believed to be in the district` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `regarded as within the district under s 43(2):` `in the district` `,` `pursued a cat or person there` `,` `performing a function there for an offence believed to be in the district` IF
        `in the district`
    ..  "(a)" ... `pursued a cat or person there`
    OR  "(b)" ... `performing a function there for an offence believed to be in the district`

§§ `Division 2 — Delegations`

§§§ `44. Delegation by local government`

-- s 44(1): "The local government may delegate to its CEO the exercise of any
-- of its powers or the discharge of any of its duties under another
-- provision of this Act." (2): "in writing"; (3): "by an absolute majority".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 44
GIVEN del IS A Delegation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a valid delegation under s 44` del IF
        del's `delegator` EQUALS `the local government`
    AND "(1)" ... del's `delegate` EQUALS `the CEO of the local government`
    AND "(2)" ... del's `in writing`
    AND "(3)" ... del's `decided by an absolute majority`

§§§ `45. Delegation by CEO of local government`

-- s 45(1): "A CEO may delegate to any employee of the local government the
-- exercise of any of the CEO's powers or the discharge of any of the CEO's
-- duties under another provision of this Act." (2): "in writing". (3)-(5):
-- conditions on a sub-delegation (a fact about the instrument, not
-- computed). (6): "A power or duty under section 63, 64 or 65 cannot be
-- delegated to an authorised person."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 45(1), (2), (6)
GIVEN del IS A Delegation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a valid delegation under s 45` del IF
        del's `delegator` EQUALS `the CEO`
    AND "(1)" ... del's `delegate` EQUALS `an employee of the local government`
    AND "(2)" ... del's `in writing`
    AND NOT "(6)" ... `a s 63, 64 or 65 power to an authorised person`
    WHERE
        `a s 63, 64 or 65 power to an authorised person` MEANS
                del's `delegate is an authorised person`
            AND elem (del's `power or duty under section`) (LIST 63, 64, 65)

§§§ `46. Other matters relevant to delegations under this Division`

-- s 46(1)(a): a delegation "has effect for the period of time specified in
-- the delegation or where no period has been specified, indefinitely";
-- (1)(b): amending or revoking a local government's delegation is "by an
-- absolute majority". s 46(2): acting through others is not prevented.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 46(1)(a)
GIVEN made      IS A DATE
      `ends on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      d         IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a delegation made on` made `and ending on` `ends on` `has effect on` d IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND d AT LEAST made
    AND CONSIDER `ends on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE          -- "indefinitely"
        WHEN JUST e  THEN d AT MOST e

§§§ `47. Register of, and review of, delegations`

-- s 47(2): "At least once every financial year, delegations made under this
-- Division are to be reviewed by the delegator." Interpretation Act s 5:
-- "financial year means the period of 12 months ending on 30 June".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 47(2); Interpretation Act 1984 s 5 "financial year"
GIVEN `the year it ends in` IS A NUMBER
      reviews              IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the delegations were reviewed in the financial year ending 30 June` `the year it ends in` `, reviewed on` reviews IF
    `the law is encoded for` (YMD `the year it ends in` 6 30)
    AND `a review in the year`
    WHERE
        `a review in the year` MEANS
            any (GIVEN r YIELD     r AT LEAST YMD (`the year it ends in` MINUS 1) 7 1
                               AND r AT MOST  YMD `the year it ends in` 6 30)
                reviews

§§ `Division 3 — Authorised persons`

-- Subdivision 1 (s 48) deleted: No. 16 of 2019 s 92. Authorised persons are
-- now the three kinds in s 3(1) (cat-part1-preliminary.l4); s 87 carries the
-- old s 48 appointees across.

§§§ `Subdivision 2 — Particular powers of authorised persons`

§§§§ `49. Authorised person may cause a cat to be destroyed`

-- s 49(1): "An authorised person may cause a cat to be destroyed in a
-- humane manner — (a) if the person believes on reasonable grounds that the
-- cat — (i) is feral, diseased or dangerous; and (ii) has caused or given,
-- or is likely to cause or give, serious injury, or serious illness, to a
-- person, another animal or itself; or (b) at the request of the owner of
-- the cat; or (c) in the circumstances, if any, prescribed." None are
-- prescribed (inputs/PROVENANCE.md).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 49(1)
GIVEN o IS AN Officer
      `believes it feral, diseased or dangerous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `believes it has caused, or is likely to cause, serious injury or illness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner requested it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 49(1) permits` o `to have the cat destroyed, given` `believes it feral, diseased or dangerous` `,` `believes it has caused, or is likely to cause, serious injury or illness` `and` `the owner requested it` IF
        `an authorised person` o
    AND (    "(a)" ... `a reasonable belief that the cat is feral, diseased or dangerous and injurious`
         ..  "(b)" ... `the owner requested it`
         OR  "(c) in the circumstances, if any, prescribed — none are" ... FALSE)
    WHERE
        `a reasonable belief that the cat is feral, diseased or dangerous and injurious` MEANS
                "(i)"  ... `believes it feral, diseased or dangerous`
            AND "(ii)" ... `believes it has caused, or is likely to cause, serious injury or illness`

-- s 49(2): "The owner of a cat destroyed under this section is liable to
-- pay to the local government that appointed or designated the authorised
-- person the reasonable costs associated with the destruction and the
-- disposal of the cat." (3): recoverable in court.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 49(2)
GIVEN `reasonable costs of destruction and disposal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the owner's s 49(2) liability, being the reasonable costs of` `reasonable costs of destruction and disposal` MEANS
    `reasonable costs of destruction and disposal`

§§§§ `50. Persons found committing breach of Act to give name on demand`

-- s 50(1): an authorised person who "(a) finds a person committing; or (b)
-- on reasonable grounds suspects a person of having committed, an offence
-- against this Act, may request from the person the person's name, place of
-- residence and date of birth." (2): "A person from whom information is
-- requested under subsection (1) must not refuse without lawful excuse to
-- give the information."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 50
GIVEN o IS AN Officer
      `found the person committing an offence`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `suspects on reasonable grounds an offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `refused to give the information`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `had a lawful excuse`                              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(2) is contravened when` o `requested, having` `found the person committing an offence` `,` `suspects on reasonable grounds an offence was committed` `; refusal` `refused to give the information` `, excuse` `had a lawful excuse` IF
        "(1)" ...     `an authorised person` o
                  AND (    "(a)" ... `found the person committing an offence`
                       OR  "(b)" ... `suspects on reasonable grounds an offence was committed`)
    AND "(2)" ...     `refused to give the information`
                  AND NOT "without lawful excuse" ... `had a lawful excuse`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 50(2) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 50(2) — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§§ `51. Power to enter premises`

-- s 51(2): the notice must "(a) state that the authorised person wishes to
-- enter the premises; and (b) specify the purpose ...; and (c) specify that
-- the owner or occupier may object to the entry and the period (being not
-- less than 24 hours) within which the objection may be made; and (d)
-- specify how the objection may be made."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 51(2)
GIVEN n IS AN `Entry notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notice in accordance with s 51(2)` n IF
        "(a)" ... n's `states the wish to enter`
    AND "(b)" ... n's `specifies the purpose`
    AND "(c)" ... n's `specifies the right to object`
              AND n's `objection period in hours` AT LEAST 24
    AND "(d)" ... n's `specifies how to object`

-- s 51(3): "(a) the notice continues to have effect until — (i) the purpose
-- for which entry was required has been effected; or (ii) 7 days after the
-- end of the objection period specified in the notice, whichever occurs
-- first; and (b) successive entries for that purpose are to be regarded as
-- entries to which the notice relates."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 51(3)
GIVEN n IS AN `Entry notice`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of effect of the entry notice` n MEANS
    IF   NOT `the law is encoded for` (n's `date the objection period ends`)
    THEN REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025"
    ELSE CONSIDER n's `date the purpose was effected`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `(ii)`
         WHEN JUST e  THEN IF e LESS THAN `(ii)` THEN e ELSE `(ii)`
    WHERE
        `(ii)` MEANS n's `date the objection period ends` PLUS 7

-- s 51(1): "In the performance of a function under this Act, an authorised
-- person may enter any premises if entry is required for the performance of
-- the function — (a) with the consent of the person who is, or appears to
-- be, the owner or occupier of the premises; or (b) if a notice has been
-- given in accordance with subsection (2) and the period specified in the
-- notice as the period within which objections may be made has elapsed with
-- no objection being made; or (c) under a warrant issued under Subdivision 3."
--
-- Dates are whole days: the objection period "has elapsed" from the day after
-- the day it ends.
DECLARE `Footing for entry` IS ONE OF
    `with consent`
    `after a notice`   HAS `the notice` IS AN `Entry notice`
    `under a warrant`
    `on no footing`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 51(1), (3)
GIVEN o IS AN Officer
      f IS A `Footing for entry`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 51(1) permits` o `to enter, on` f `, on` d IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `an authorised person` o
    AND CONSIDER f
        WHEN `with consent`     THEN TRUE                                                     -- (a)
        WHEN `after a notice` n THEN     `a notice in accordance with s 51(2)` n              -- (b)
                                     AND NOT n's `objection made`
                                     AND d GREATER THAN n's `date the objection period ends`
                                     AND d AT MOST `the last day of effect of the entry notice` n
        WHEN `under a warrant`  THEN TRUE                                                     -- (c)
        WHEN `on no footing`    THEN FALSE

§§§§ `52. General powers of authorised person`

-- s 52: the powers, a list (a)-(c)(iv). INERT: each is a permission whose
-- exercise is a judgement on the ground.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 52
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 52 — general powers of an authorised person` MEANS
    LIST "(a) set traps for cats in or on any public place or any premises lawfully entered"
       , "(b) examine, including by scanning, a cat to determine if the cat is the subject of an offence against this Act"
       , "(c)(i) in any premises lawfully entered ... examine, seize, copy or take extracts from any documents relevant to the offence"
       , "(c)(ii) ... take photographs, films and audio, video or other recordings relevant to the offence"
       , "(c)(iii) ... direct a person to answer questions"
       , "(c)(iv) ... take any other action that the authorised person believes, on reasonable grounds, is necessary"

§§§§ `53. Act does not derogate from powers of police officers`

-- s 53: "Nothing in this Act derogates from the powers of an authorised
-- person who is a police officer." INERT: a saving.

§§§§ `54. Obstruction`

-- s 54: "A person must not delay, threaten, obstruct or otherwise hinder an
-- authorised person in the performance of a function by that person under
-- this Act."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 54
GIVEN o IS AN Officer
      `delayed, threatened, obstructed or otherwise hindered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer was performing a function under this Act`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 54 is contravened against` o `, the person having` `delayed, threatened, obstructed or otherwise hindered` `, the officer` `the officer was performing a function under this Act` IF
        `an authorised person` o
    AND `the officer was performing a function under this Act`
    AND `delayed, threatened, obstructed or otherwise hindered`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 54 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 54 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `Subdivision 3 — Warrants`

§§§§ `55-56. Grounds for warrants`

-- s 55: "A justice may issue a warrant authorising an authorised person to
-- enter premises if satisfied, by an application supported by evidence on
-- oath, that — (a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there is
-- at the premises anything that may afford evidence of the commission of an
-- offence against this Act; or (b) entry onto the premises is reasonably
-- required to investigate a suspected offence against this Act."
-- A power of the justice: TRUE means the justice MAY issue.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 55
GIVEN `supported by evidence on oath`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable grounds to suspect evidence there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entry reasonably required to investigate`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a justice may issue a s 55 search warrant, on oath` `supported by evidence on oath` `, where` `reasonable grounds to suspect evidence there` `or` `entry reasonably required to investigate` IF
        `supported by evidence on oath`
    AND (    "(a)" ... `reasonable grounds to suspect evidence there`
         OR  "(b)" ... `entry reasonably required to investigate`)

-- s 56: "... to seize a cat, or cats, if satisfied, by an application
-- supported by evidence on oath, that there are reasonable grounds for
-- suspecting that the cat is, or cats are, the subject of an offence, or
-- offences, against this Act."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 56
GIVEN `supported by evidence on oath`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable grounds to suspect the cat is the subject of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a justice may issue a s 56 warrant to seize, on oath` `supported by evidence on oath` `, where` `reasonable grounds to suspect the cat is the subject of an offence` IF
        `supported by evidence on oath`
    AND `reasonable grounds to suspect the cat is the subject of an offence`

§§§§ `57-60. Applying for, and executing, a warrant`

-- s 57(1): a warrant may be sought even where entry or seizure without one
-- is lawful; (2): the Criminal Investigation Act 2006 s 13 applies. s 58 and
-- reg 26: Form 5. s 59: "A warrant comes into force when it is issued by a
-- justice." s 60(1): executed by "(a) the authorised person to whom it is
-- issued; or (b) a person specified on the warrant; or (c) any other
-- authorised person"; (2): produced on reasonable request.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 60(1)
GIVEN `the person it was issued to`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person specified on it`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorised person`             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 60(1) lets the person execute the warrant:` `the person it was issued to` `,` `a person specified on it` `,` `an authorised person` IF
        "(a)" ... `the person it was issued to`
    ..  "(b)" ... `a person specified on it`
    OR  "(c)" ... `an authorised person`

§§ `Division 4 — Infringement notices`

§§§ `Schedule 2 — Modified penalties (reg 30, s 63(2))`

-- reg 30: "The penalties set out in Schedule 2 column 4 are the prescribed
-- modified penalties for the offences in columns 2 and 3 to which the
-- penalties correspond, for the purposes of section 63(2) of the Act."
-- Fourteen items, each $200. An offence the Schedule does not list is not
-- prescribed BY THESE REGULATIONS; under s 61 a local law may also prescribe
-- an offence against the Act, so the absence is named, not read as "never".
DECLARE `Prescription for infringement` IS ONE OF
    `prescribed in Schedule 2` HAS `the item` IS A NUMBER
                                   `the modified penalty` IS A NUMBER
    `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it`

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 30, Sch 2
GIVEN o IS AN Offence
GIVETH A `Prescription for infringement`
`the Schedule 2 entry for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    --                                                                                     item  penalty
    WHEN `s 5(1) — cat not registered`                                     THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2`  1  200
    WHEN `s 6(1) — registered cat in a public place not wearing its tag`   THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2`  2  200
    WHEN `s 7 — removing or interfering with a registration tag`           THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2`  3  200
    WHEN `s 14(1) — cat not microchipped`                                  THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2`  4  200
    WHEN `s 17 — removing or interfering with a microchip`                 THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2`  5  200
    WHEN `s 18(1) — cat not sterilised`                                    THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2`  6  200
    WHEN `s 19 — identifying as sterilised a cat that is not`              THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2`  7  200
    WHEN `s 23(1) — transferring a cat that is not microchipped`           THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2`  8  200
    WHEN `s 23(2) — transferring a cat that is not sterilised`             THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2`  9  200
    WHEN `s 24 — seller not giving notice of a transfer`                   THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2` 10  200
    WHEN `s 25 — owner not giving notice of a change to recorded information` THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2` 11  200
    WHEN `s 35(1) — breeding cats without approval`                        THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2` 12  200
    WHEN `s 41 — offering a cat as a prize`                                THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2` 13  200
    WHEN `s 50(2) — refusing to give name, residence and date of birth`    THEN `prescribed in Schedule 2` 14  200
    OTHERWISE `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it`

-- Every offence in the Act and Regulations carries "Penalty: a fine of
-- $5 000." (each module repeats it beside its section).
@ref Cat Act 2011, every "Penalty:" line; Cat Regulations 2012 reg 5(2), (3)
GIVEN o IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` o MEANS 5000

§§§ `61-63. Giving an infringement notice`

-- s 63(3): "A modified penalty for an offence must not exceed 10% of the
-- maximum penalty for that offence."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 63(3)
GIVEN o IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 63(3) is met by the modified penalty for` o IF
    CONSIDER `the Schedule 2 entry for` o
    WHEN `prescribed in Schedule 2` i amount THEN amount AT MOST `the maximum fine for` o TIMES 10%
    WHEN `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it` THEN TRUE

-- s 62(1): "An authorised person who has reason to believe that a person
-- has committed a prescribed offence against this Act or a regulation or
-- local law made under this Act may, within 28 days after the alleged
-- offence is believed to have been committed, give an infringement notice
-- to the alleged offender." s 62(3): "A person who is not an employee of a
-- local government cannot be appointed to be an authorised person for the
-- purposes of this section." s 63(2): the modified penalty specified "is to
-- be the amount that was the prescribed modified penalty at the time the
-- alleged offence is believed to have been committed."
--
-- `local law penalty` is the modified penalty a local law prescribes for
-- the offence, if one does; Schedule 2 is consulted first. Only offences
-- against the Act are listed in the Offence type's Schedule 2 rows.
@ref Cat Act 2011 ss 62(1), (3), 63(2)
GIVEN o                   IS AN Officer
      n                   IS AN `Infringement notice`
      offence             IS AN Offence
      `local law penalty` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      holidays            IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 62 permits` o `to give notice` n `for` offence `, a local law prescribing` `local law penalty` `given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` (n's `date of the alleged offence`)
    AND `an authorised person` o
    AND "(3)" ... o's `an employee of the local government`
    AND "(1) a prescribed offence" ... `prescribed`
    AND "(1) within 28 days after the alleged offence"
        ... n's `date given` AT MOST `the last day to act within` 28 `days after` (n's `date of the alleged offence`) `given` holidays
    AND "s 63(2)" ... n's `modified penalty specified` EQUALS `the prescribed modified penalty`
    WHERE
        `prescribed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Schedule 2 entry for` offence
            WHEN `prescribed in Schedule 2` i amount THEN TRUE
            WHEN `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it` THEN
                CONSIDER `local law penalty`
                WHEN JUST x  THEN TRUE
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        `the prescribed modified penalty` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Schedule 2 entry for` offence
            WHEN `prescribed in Schedule 2` i amount THEN amount
            WHEN `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it` THEN
                CONSIDER `local law penalty`
                WHEN JUST x  THEN x
                WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "the offence is not prescribed for an infringement notice by Schedule 2, and no local-law modified penalty was supplied"

-- s 62(2): "A local government can only prescribe an offence for the
-- purposes of subsection (1) if a prosecution for the offence could be
-- commenced by the local government or any of its employees and the local
-- government is satisfied that — (a) commission of the offence would be a
-- relatively minor matter; and (b) only straightforward issues of law and
-- fact would be involved ...".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 62(2)
GIVEN `the local government could prosecute`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `relatively minor`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `only straightforward issues`             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a local government may prescribe the offence under s 62(2):` `the local government could prosecute` `,` `relatively minor` `,` `only straightforward issues` IF
        `the local government could prosecute`
    AND "(a)" ... `relatively minor`
    AND "(b)" ... `only straightforward issues`

§§§ `64-66. Paying, extending and withdrawing`

-- s 63(1)(b): the modified penalty "may be paid ... within a period of 28
-- days after the giving of the notice". s 64: the CEO "may, in a particular
-- case, extend the period of 28 days ... whether or not the period of 28
-- days has elapsed."
@ref Cat Act 2011 ss 63(1)(b), 64
GIVEN n        IS AN `Infringement notice`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay the modified penalty under` n `given` holidays MEANS
    IF   NOT `the law is encoded for` (n's `date given`)
    THEN REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025"
    ELSE `the last day to act within` (28 PLUS n's `extended time to pay, in days`) `days after` (n's `date given`) `given` holidays

-- s 65(1): "Within one year after the notice was given the CEO of the local
-- government may, whether or not the modified penalty has been paid,
-- withdraw an infringement notice". (2): a paid penalty is refunded.
-- The year is reckoned after the day of giving (Interpretation Act s 61(1)(b),
-- s 62); if its last day is an excluded day, the withdrawal may be made on the
-- next day that is not (s 61(1)(e)) — as for every other time limit here.
-- (Added 2026-10-05 after the independent test pass; NOTES.md section 5.)
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 65(1); Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(b), (e)
GIVEN d        IS A DATE
      n        IS AN `Infringement notice`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on` d `the CEO may withdraw` n `given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` (n's `date given`)
    AND d AT LEAST n's `date given`
    AND d AT MOST `the first day from` `the last day of the year` `that is not excluded, given` holidays
    WHERE
        `the last day of the year` MEANS
            `the day after a period of` 12 `months beginning on` (n's `date given` PLUS 1) MINUS 1

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 65(2)
GIVEN n IS AN `Infringement notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65(2) requires a refund under` n IF
    CONSIDER n's `date withdrawn`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST w  THEN CONSIDER n's `date paid`
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                      WHEN JUST p  THEN p AT MOST w

-- s 66(1)-(2): "if the modified penalty specified in an infringement notice
-- has been paid within 28 days or such further time as is allowed and the
-- notice has not been withdrawn", proceedings and penalties are barred as
-- if the offender had been convicted and punished. (3): payment is not an
-- admission.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 66(1), (2)
GIVEN n        IS AN `Infringement notice`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paying under` n `bars proceedings for the offence, given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` (n's `date given`)
    AND `paid in time`
    AND `not withdrawn`
    WHERE
        `paid in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER n's `date paid`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST p  THEN p AT MOST `the last day to pay the modified penalty under` n `given` holidays
        `not withdrawn` MEANS
            CONSIDER n's `date withdrawn`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST w  THEN FALSE

-- s 67: "An amount paid as a modified penalty is, subject to section 65(2),
-- to be dealt with as if it were a fine imposed by a court as a penalty for
-- an offence." INERT here.

§§ `Division 5 — Objections and review`

§§§ `68. When this Division applies`

-- s 68: refusal to grant or renew registration (s 9); cancellation of
-- registration (s 10); refusal to approve or renew an approval to breed
-- (s 37); cancellation of an approval to breed (s 38).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 68
GIVEN dec IS A `Reviewable decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 5 applies to` dec IF
    NOT dec EQUALS `another decision`

§§§ `69. Objection may be lodged`

-- s 69(1): "A person who has been given notice under section 13 or 40 of a
-- decision may object to the decision if the person has not applied for a
-- review of the decision under this Division." s 69(2): "... within 28 days
-- after the right of objection arose, or within such further time as the
-- local government may allow." The right arises when the notice is given.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 69(2)
GIVEN h        IS AN `Objection history`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to object to the decision in` h `given` holidays MEANS
    CONSIDER h's `date notice of the decision was given`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING          -- no notice, no right of objection yet
    WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`the last day to act within` (28 PLUS h's `further time allowed by the local government, in days`) `days after` n `given` holidays)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 69
GIVEN h        IS AN `Objection history`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objection in` h `was lodged in time, given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` (h's `date of the decision`)
    AND `Division 5 applies to` (h's `decision`)
    AND `no review applied for before it`
    AND CONSIDER h's `date objection lodged`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST l  THEN CONSIDER `the last day to object to the decision in` h `given` holidays
                          WHEN NOTHING    THEN FALSE
                          WHEN JUST last  THEN l AT MOST last
    WHERE
        `no review applied for before it` MEANS
            CONSIDER h's `date review applied for`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST r  THEN CONSIDER h's `date objection lodged`
                              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                              WHEN JUST l  THEN r GREATER THAN l

§§§ `70. Dealing with objection`

-- s 70: the council or an authorised committee deals with it, but "A
-- committee cannot deal with an objection against a decision that it made or
-- a decision that the council made"; the objector may make submissions;
-- disposal is by (a) dismissal, (b) variation or (c) revocation, with or
-- without substitution or referral; written notice of the disposal and the
-- reasons is to be given.
DECLARE `Body dealing with an objection` IS ONE OF
    `the council`
    `a committee authorised by the council`

DECLARE `Maker of the decision` IS ONE OF
    `made by the council`
    `made by that committee`
    `made by someone else`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 70(1), (2)
GIVEN b IS A `Body dealing with an objection`
      m IS A `Maker of the decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 70 lets` b `deal with an objection to a decision` m IF
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN `the council`                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a committee authorised by the council` THEN m EQUALS `made by someone else`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 70(4)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 70(4) — ways to dispose of an objection` MEANS
    LIST "(a) dismissing the objection"
       , "(b) varying the decision objected to"
       , "(c)(i) revoking the decision objected to, substituting for it another decision"
       , "(c)(ii) revoking the decision objected to, referring the matter, with or without directions, for another decision by a committee or person whose function it is to make such a decision"
       , "(c) revoking the decision objected to, with neither substitution nor referral"

§§§ `71. Review of decisions`

-- s 71(1): review by the State Administrative Tribunal "if the person — (a)
-- has not lodged an objection to the decision; or (b) has lodged an
-- objection but, at the expiration of 35 days after it was lodged, has not
-- been given notice in writing of how it has been decided to dispose of the
-- objection." (2): after a disposal notice, review "of the decision on the
-- objection". (3): "The application is to be made within 42 days after the
-- right to make it arose." The section's examples: "(a) within 42 days after
-- the original decision, for an application under subsection (1)(a); or (b)
-- more than 35 days, but within 77 days, after the objection was lodged, for
-- an application under subsection (1)(b); or (c) within 42 days after the
-- objection was decided, for an application under subsection (2)."
--
-- FORK F-16: under (1)(a) the right arises when notice of the decision is
-- given — (1) gives it only to "A person who has been given notice under
-- section 13 or 40". Example (a) says "after the original decision"; the
-- two agree when notice is given on the day of the decision, and the notice
-- date governs where they differ.
DECLARE `Review window` HAS
    `route`               IS A STRING
    `first day`           IS A DATE
    `last day`            IS A DATE

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 71
GIVEN h        IS AN `Objection history`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Review window`
`the s 71 review window for` h `given` holidays MEANS
    IF   NOT `the law is encoded for` (h's `date of the decision`)
    THEN REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025"
    ELSE `the window, where Division 5 applies`
    WHERE
        `the window, where Division 5 applies` MEANS
            IF NOT `Division 5 applies to` (h's `decision`)
            THEN NOTHING
            ELSE CONSIDER h's `date objection lodged`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN                                                              -- (1)(a)
                     CONSIDER h's `date notice of the decision was given`
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                     WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`Review window` WITH
                                                `route`     IS "s 71(1)(a): no objection lodged"
                                                `first day` IS n
                                                `last day`  IS `the last day to act within` 42 `days after` n `given` holidays)
                 WHEN JUST l THEN
                     CONSIDER h's `date notice of disposal of the objection given`
                     WHEN JUST disposed THEN                                                     -- (2), or (1)(b) if disposal came late
                         IF   disposed AT MOST (l PLUS 35)
                         THEN JUST (`Review window` WITH
                                       `route`     IS "s 71(2): review of the decision on the objection"
                                       `first day` IS disposed
                                       `last day`  IS `the last day to act within` 42 `days after` disposed `given` holidays)
                         ELSE JUST (`(1)(b) window from` l)
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`(1)(b) window from` l)                             -- (1)(b)
        `(1)(b) window from` l MEANS
            `Review window` WITH
                `route`     IS "s 71(1)(b): objection not disposed of within 35 days"
                `first day` IS l PLUS 36
                `last day`  IS `the last day to act within` 42 `days after` (l PLUS 35) `given` holidays

§§§ `72. Suspension of effect of some decisions`

-- s 72: "If an objection has been lodged, or an application for review made
-- under this Division against a decision to — (a) refuse to renew the
-- registration of a cat under section 9; or (b) cancel the registration of
-- a cat under section 10; or (c) refuse to renew the approval for a person
-- to breed cats under section 37; or (d) cancel the approval for a person to
-- breed cats under section 38, the effect of the decision is suspended, and
-- the registration or approval, as is relevant, is to be taken to continue
-- to have effect pending the determination of the application unless the
-- State Administrative Tribunal orders that the effect of the decision
-- should not be suspended." A refusal to GRANT is not listed: there is
-- nothing to continue.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 72
GIVEN h                          IS AN `Objection history`
      `still pending`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Tribunal ordered no suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision in` h `is suspended, pending:` `still pending` `, Tribunal order against:` `the Tribunal ordered no suspension` IF
        `the law is encoded for` (h's `date of the decision`)
    AND "(a)-(d)" ... `a decision s 72 lists`
    AND `an objection or application has been made`
    AND `still pending`
    AND NOT `the Tribunal ordered no suspension`
    WHERE
        `a decision s 72 lists` MEANS
                "(a)" ... h's `decision` EQUALS `refusal to renew registration`
            ..  "(b)" ... h's `decision` EQUALS `cancellation of registration`
            ..  "(c)" ... h's `decision` EQUALS `refusal to renew an approval to breed`
            OR  "(d)" ... h's `decision` EQUALS `cancellation of an approval to breed`
        `an objection or application has been made` MEANS
            CONSIDER h's `date objection lodged`
            WHEN JUST l  THEN TRUE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN CONSIDER h's `date review applied for`
                              WHEN JUST r  THEN TRUE
                              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§§ `Division 6 — Legal proceedings`

§§§ `73. Prosecutions`

-- s 73(1): for an offence against the Act, "(a) a person who is acting in
-- the course of his or her duties as an employee of a local government;
-- (b) a person who is authorised to do so by a local government." (2): the
-- same for a local law, but of "the local government that made the local
-- law". (3): authority and signature need no proof unless evidence is
-- given to the contrary.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 73(1)
GIVEN `acting as an employee of a local government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorised by a local government`            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may prosecute an offence against the Act:` `acting as an employee of a local government` `,` `authorised by a local government` IF
        "(a)" ... `acting as an employee of a local government`
    OR  "(b)" ... `authorised by a local government`

§§§ `74. Additional court orders`

-- s 74(1): "If — (a) a court convicts a person of an offence against this
-- Act; and (b) the person has previously been convicted of 2 or more
-- offences against this Act, the court may, in addition to imposing any
-- other penalty imposed under this Act, order — (c) that the person is
-- banned from owning or keeping a cat permanently or for the period
-- specified in the order; or (d) that ... the person is to take immediate
-- action to ensure that any, or all, cats owned by the person ... are — (i)
-- microchipped; or (ii) sterilised, or both." A power of the court.
-- Fork F-07 applies: offences against the Act itself.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 74(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Conviction before the court`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an additional order under s 74 on` c IF
        `the law is encoded for` (c's `date of the conviction`)
    AND "(a)" ... c's `against the Act`
    AND "(b)" ... count (filter `a previous conviction against this Act` (c's `offender`'s `convictions`)) AT LEAST 2
    WHERE
        `a previous conviction against this Act` x MEANS
                x's `offence against` EQUALS `the Cat Act 2011`
            AND x's `instrument` EQUALS `the Act itself`
            AND x's `date of the conviction` LESS THAN c's `date of the conviction`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 74(1)(c), (d)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 74(1) — the orders available` MEANS
    LIST "(c) that the person is banned from owning or keeping a cat permanently or for the period specified in the order"
       , "(d)(i) that the person is to take immediate action to ensure that any, or all, cats owned by the person are microchipped"
       , "(d)(ii) that the person is to take immediate action to ensure that any, or all, cats owned by the person are sterilised"

§§§ `75. Evidentiary matters`

-- s 75(1): an allegation in the prosecution notice that, at a specified
-- time, any of (a)-(k) existed "is taken to be proved in the absence of
-- evidence to the contrary". A presumption about proof, not a rule of
-- substance: the matters are listed so a reader can find them.
-- s 75(3): "in addition to ... the Evidence Act 1906" — to read "Evidence
-- Act 2025" from 18 September 2027 (inputs/PROVENANCE.md); no computed
-- answer changes.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 75(1)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 75(1) — matters taken to be proved` MEANS
    LIST "(a) that a specified cat was not registered"
       , "(b) that a specified person was the registered owner of a specified cat"
       , "(c) that a specified person's name was recorded as the owner of a specified cat in a microchip database"
       , "(d) that a specified person ordinarily kept and cared for a specified cat"
       , "(e) that a specified cat was ordinarily kept in the district of a specified local government"
       , "(f) that a specified person was the owner of a specified cat"
       , "(g) that a specified database was a microchip database"
       , "(h) that a specified person or body was a microchip database company"
       , "(i) that a specified cat was not sterilised"
       , "(j) that a specified cat was not microchipped"
       , "(k) that a specified cat had reached 6 months of age"

-- regs 26-29: the forms. Warrant: Form 5 (s 58). Infringement notice:
-- Form 6 (s 63(1)). Withdrawal: Form 7 (s 65(1)). Objection: Form 8 (s 69(2)).
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 regs 26-29
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`regs 26-29 — prescribed forms` MEANS
    LIST "reg 26: warrant (s 58) — Form 5"
       , "reg 27: infringement notice (s 63(1)) — Form 6"
       , "reg 28: withdrawal of infringement notice (s 65(1)) — Form 7"
       , "reg 29: objection (s 69(2)) — Form 8"
